## 6. Change control

Any request that adds, removes or alters a deliverable, a criterion, the
timeline or approved strategy is raised as a change order with scope, fee,
schedule impact and acceptance criteria. Work on a change starts only after
written approval. Small changes may be absorbed only when both parties record
them as such in the decision log.

## 7. Client responsibilities

- One named decision-maker and one feedback consolidator.
- Source material, access and content by the dates in section 4.
- Consolidated feedback within the agreed review window.
- Licences or approvals the client must hold (trade-mark clearance, regulated claims, third-party content).

